@startuml
' purpose: what a harness.manifest declares, and which reader consumes each field
' covers: internal/manifest/**
' covers: defs/*/harness.manifest
' covers: embed.go
'
' ── F10 (DONE (wt) 2026-10-17): NO `docker:` KEY; `daemon:` IS THE ONE KNOB ─
' Part of the user's "apply fixes for SEC2, SEC3, N1, F18, F10, …"
' (repo-simplification.puml F10, option 1). MEASURED: Manifest.Docker,
' DockerMode, its constants and IsSbx are deleted, and no defs/*/harness.manifest
' declares `docker:`. Every harness runs in sbx, so the key said nothing.
' `daemon:` (Daemon *bool, manifest.go:72) is the only daemon knob:
' WantsDocker() = Daemon == nil || *Daemon (:82-84) — hermes's `daemon: false`
' is the one def that withdraws the daemon; e2e/sbx_test.go builds its
' docker-access matrix from WantsDocker (:131-132). Parse decodes with yaml
' KnownFields(true) (:301), so a STALE key fails loading and names itself; a
' stale `docker:` also gets the repair: "`docker:` is retired — delete it, or
' set `daemon: false` to withdraw the daemon" (:304, added after the adversarial
' review). TestAStaleManifestKeyFailsLoading (manifest_test.go) pins `docker:
' sbx` with that hint, `egress: true` and `provider: cursor`;
' TestDaemonIsTheOneDaemonKnob pins the three daemon cases.
' OPEN (repo-simplification.puml N20): nothing in the PRODUCT reads `daemon:` —
' WantsDocker's only caller is the e2e matrix — and the picker still promises a
' `daemon: false` harness "a microVM with its own Docker daemon" (internal/run/
' choices.go:508). OPEN (SEC4): Home.validate accepts a home mount `host: .`
' (manifest.go:257-291), which would bind the whole proveo home.
' Deleted as tautologies with the key (reported):
' TestDockerModeAcceptsOnlyTheSandbox, TestDockerModePredicatesAreExhaustive,
' TestDaemonFalseKeepsTheSandboxAndWithdrawsTheDaemon,
' TestEveryDaemonPromiseIsTheSandbox, TestEveryHarnessRunsInTheSandbox,
' TestSubscriptionHarnessesRunOnTheSandboxBackend,
' TestCursorTakesDockerFromTheSandboxBackend, TestManifestIgnoresUnknownTopLevelKeys
' (KnownFields contradicts it), TestEveryDaemonPromiseIsCoveredBySbx (e2e) and
' TestAddonOptionsOffersTheDockerSandbox. The note on M below keeps the history.
' F19 (2026-10-17): a home mount may omit `container:` — a direct bind at its
' host path; container duplicates are checked only when one is set
' (manifest.go:273-288; TestAHomeMountMayOmitItsContainerPath, manifest_test.go:366;
' _spec/defs/hermes/hermes-persistence.puml).
' ── agentEnv IS A THIRD KIND OF VARIABLE, AND THE DISTINCTION MATTERS ──────
' NAME: value pairs handed to the agent on EVERY backend unless the operator
' sets NAME themselves. It is neither `env` — variables the OPERATOR supplies,
' prompted for when missing and hinted about when auth fails — nor `config`,
' which forwards a host preference only when one exists.
'
' It exists because a default exported by the image entrypoint reached only the
' docker backend: sbx launches the agent through its own kit and never runs the
' entrypoint. Delivered as an ARGV on both backends, and the pairs come out in
' NAME ORDER because the plan goldens read that argv. The field cannot
' double-declare a name `env` or `config` already claims, and nothing may
' default to empty.
'
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title harness.manifest — the single registration point (schema)

class "Manifest\ndefs/<name>/harness.manifest" as M <<app>> {
  name : string
  description : string
  --
  daemon : bool  (absent → true; false withdraws the daemon)
  subscription : bool
  stability : experimental|candidate|stable
  --
  images : map[target]imageRef
  --
  Dir : string  (set by Load, not YAML)
}

class "Workspace\nworkspace:" as W <<app>> {
  layout : app
  configDir : string
  gitMode : rw | ro
  output : bool
  mode : rw | ro
}

class "Home\nhome:" as H <<app>> {
  enabled : bool
}

class "HomeMount\nhome.mounts[]" as HM <<db>> {
  host : string  (relative to PROVEO_HOME)
  container : string  (absolute; optional — absent = a direct bind)
  mode : rw | ro
  deny : []string  (basenames scrubbed each run)
}

class "EnvVar\nenv[]" as E <<error>> {
  name : string
  description : string
  secret : bool
}

class "config[]" as C <<app>> {
  names of NON-SECRET host preferences
  forwarded by value (-e NAME=value)
}

class "agentEnv\nagentEnv:" as AE <<app>> {
  NAME : value  (proveo's defaults for the agent)
  forwarded on EVERY backend (-e NAME=value)
  the operator's own value wins
}

M *-- W
M *-- H
H *-- HM
M *-- E
M *-- C
M *-- AE

note right of M
  **Adding a harness = dropping a def dir + this file.**
  Everything else enumerates from it: runnable targets,
  image refs, mount model, the daemon offer, auth
  prompts, build/test/deploy registry.
  **Two keys left 2026-10-16 (MEASURED):** ""egress: true""
  (Manifest.Egress, "sources the egress lifecycle") and
  ""provider: cursor"" (Manifest.Provider, the docker
  broker's vendor pin). Nothing read either. Vendor
  pinning lives only in ""capabilities.providers"".
  **No ""docker:"" key since F10 (2026-10-17).** Every harness runs
  in sbx, so the key carried no information; a stale one now fails
  loading by name (KnownFields). HISTORY: ""docker:"" was an ENUM
  with one value left, ""sbx"" — a missing one loaded and ""proveo
  run"" refused with "does not declare `docker: sbx`"; before
  2026-10-17 ""docker: dind"" had its own refusal, and stale
  ""dind:"" / ""sandbox_docker:"" / ""egress:"" / ""provider:"" keys
  loaded silently.

  **""daemon: false"" is the one daemon knob.** hermes is a general
  assistant, not a coding agent, on an upstream base with no Docker
  Engine, so it keeps the sandbox and withdraws the daemon (decided
  2026-09-29). ""WantsDocker"" = ""daemon"" absent or true, and the
  docker-access matrix iterates it.

  **The promise is asserted for EVERY def that makes it, and
  there is now one way to assert it.** The e2e matrix
  (""TestEveryHarnessGetsTheDockerAccessItPromises"") is derived
  from the manifests and runs one probe: a ""WantsDocker"" def must
  REACH a daemon inside its sandbox. That verdict is INVERTED
  from the one it replaces, which required the sandbox to reach
  none — true while no proveo image carried
  ""com.docker.sandboxes.start-docker"" and false since.

  The boundary half moved rather than vanished:
  ""e2e/sbx_egress_test\.go"" fails when a pull from inside the
  sandbox reaches a registry no Kit allowlists, which is the
  property the five dind gates used to buy by refusing the
  daemon outright.

  The docker CLIENT is no longer asserted up front on either
  side: its survival is an sbx implementation detail that
  differs between our own two images
  (""_spec/_experiments/docker-sandbox\.puml""), so pinning it
  would encode that detail as a proveo contract. A missing one
  is still named when it bites, because
  ""assertDockerServerReachable"" separates "command not found"
  from "cannot connect".

  Splitting it into two tests over two hardcoded lists is what
  hid the gap this replaced: the sbx half silently SKIPPED on
  every host without the CLI, so ""docker: sbx"" was an unasserted
  claim for as long as it took someone to install ""sbx"".
  ""TestEveryDaemonPromiseIsCoveredBySbx"" kept that guard until
  F10 deleted it as a tautology (every harness is sbx now); the
  matrix itself still fails when empty ("no def promises a docker
  daemon — the matrix cannot be empty", e2e/sbx_test.go:456-457).

  Validated by ""Manifest.Validate"" at load, after a strict
  decode (KnownFields: an unknown key fails); ""Targets""
  flattens ""images"" across defs and rejects a duplicate
  target name.

  Loaded from disk (""Load"") or from the binary's
  embedded copy (""LoadFS"" + ""embed.go""), so the CLI
  works with no defs tree present.

  **Which of the two ""cmd/proveo"" picks is an override, not
  a search.** ""loadManifests"" reads the manifests embedded in
  the binary, and reads a working-tree defs dir instead when
  ""PROVEO_DEFS_DIR"" is set. That env var exists for dev
  iteration: a def can be edited and run without rebuilding
  the binary to re-embed it.
end note

note bottom of W
  ""layout"" drives ""internal/workspace"":
  * **app** — repo (or scope subdir) at ""/app"", ""-w /app"";
    monorepo case also binds root ""/app/.git"", the
    ""rootFiles"" allowlist and ""configDir""
  * **app** — ""/app"" +
    ""/app/output"", no ""-w""
  ""mode:ro"" makes the tree read-only; ""output:true"" adds
  ""/app/output"".
end note

note bottom of HM
  The **only** durable state across a ""--rm"" run.
  ""deny"" is a security control, not hygiene — see
  _spec/internal/proveohome/proveo-home-components.puml
end note

note bottom of E
  Declared env the harness reads. ""secret:true"" is never
  put on an argv: under broker sbx's secret store holds
  the real value; under forward it travels by name
  (bare ""-e NAME""). The docker tiers' sentinel is gone.
end note

note bottom of C
  The **non-secret** counterpart to ""env"": these are
  forwarded BY VALUE onto the docker argv, on top of the
  shared baseline in ""entrypoint.ConfigVars"" (the model +
  UI aliases every def bridges — see
  _spec/internal/entrypoint/model-alias-bridges.puml).

  Because the value lands on an argv in plain sight,
  ""Validate"" rejects a manifest that lists a name already
  declared in ""env"" — a secret must stay on sbx's
  secret-store path, never here.
end note

note bottom of AE
  **proveo's opinion, not the operator's input.** ""env"" is what the
  operator supplies and is prompted for when missing; ""config"" forwards
  a host preference only when one exists; ""agentEnv"" lands a value the
  harness should run with unless the operator says otherwise, in name
  order so the plan argv is stable.

  It exists because a default exported by the image entrypoint reaches
  only the docker backend: sbx launches the agent through its own kit
  and never runs the entrypoint, so claudecode came up in whatever
  renderer its saved ""tui"" setting named. ""Validate"" rejects a name
  also declared in ""env"" or ""config"", and an empty value — that is the
  unset state, not a default.
end note

class "Capabilities\ncapabilities:" as CAP <<app>> {
  credentials []string
  providers []string
}

M *-- CAP

note bottom of CAP
  **The per-def choice matrix** — the only source of truth for which
  cells of the credentials/provider space a harness supports.
  An empty list means unconstrained.

  * ""providers: [anthropic]"" — claudecode reads only its own key and
    OAuth token

  //HISTORY, removed 2026-10-16 ("Drop the pins"):// ""Capabilities.Egress""
  is deleted, and cursor's ""egress: [open]"" and ""credentials: [forward]""
  pins are dropped — they encoded the docker-egress truth that its pinned TLS
  defeated interception. On sbx the proxy brokers cursor natively. The
  top-level ""egress: true"" and ""provider: cursor"" keys and their fields
  (Manifest.Egress, Manifest.Provider) are deleted too; ""providers"" is the
  one vendor pin left (MEASURED; repo-simplification.puml F10).

  ""providers"" is not cosmetic. Provider detection is filtered through
  it, so a key the harness could never use never enters sbx's store.
  (On the deleted docker broker, two or more detected keys made it refuse
  to pin and the agent got the ""proveo-brokered"" sentinel and a 403.)

  Declaring the matrix here replaced target-name special cases in
  ""cmd/proveo"". An axis the operator did not name is defaulted to the
  def's single allowed value; an axis they did name is refused with the
  reason rather than silently rewritten.
end note

note bottom of M
  **One registration point: adding a harness should mean dropping a def
  directory in, not editing the CLI.** Everything the host needs to run a
  target is declared here rather than discovered by target name.

  ""layout"" is now a single value, ""app"": the repo at ""/app"", the monorepo
  shape every def shares. It once also took ""input-output"" — claudecode's
  ""/workspace/input"" plus ""/workspace/output"" — which was the only reason
  ""ScopeRel"" returned early and left that harness without sub-project scope.
  Retiring it standardised the mount model AND handed claudecode the scoping
  the others already had; a writable output dir is now declared by
  ""output: true"" instead of implied by the layout.

  ""env"" declares variables the harness reads at run time, which is what
  lets the CLI both forward them and prompt for a missing one. ""config"" is
  the non-secret counterpart, forwarded **by value** on top of the shared
  baseline. ""hosts"" are endpoints the **harness itself** needs — a model
  catalog, a plugin registry — infrastructure rather than agent-initiated
  egress, so they are never brokered. Since 2026-10-16 they are no longer
  written into the sbx Kit allowlist; ""sandbox.ReachHosts"" names them in the
  ""sbx policy allow network"" hint instead (_spec/internal/sbx/policy-baseline.puml).

  ""home"" declares durable proveo-owned mounts under ""PROVEO_HOME"", with
  Host relative to it and Container absolute; declaring at least one is
  what activates ""HOME=/proveo-home"" so the harness's own tools write
  where the run can keep them.
end note


@enduml
